<title>ESTONIA: UHIS RUSSIA LEASING ARM GETS LICENCE.</title>
<headline>UHIS RUSSIA LEASING ARM GETS LICENCE.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uhispank's Russian leasing subsidiary has been issued a two-year licence to operate in St Petersburg, Uhisliising said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>In a statement, Uhispank said its year-end forecast for the Russia leasing firm was for a leasing portfolio volume worth 200 million kroons.</p>
<p>Russia Uhisliising is 75 percent owned by Uhispank and 25 percent owned by a Petersburg company, Neva Rus.</p>
<p>Russia Uhisliising's managing director Andrei Haponen said in statement that the company will be following a conservative plan, despite a market with a big future.</p>
<p>He added that his firm did not wish to take big risks.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
